# sha256 of every version of every synced validator HITL has shipped, under every plugin tag on
# both lines (hitl--v1.* and hitl--v2.*), plus the tree at each release since.
#
# dev-update (migrate_project.py --sync-validators) treats a repo copy that differs from the
# shipped file as the repo's own edit and keeps it. That rule cannot tell an edit from an older
# shipped version left behind by an earlier update, and plugin #35 was the result: a 2.10 review
# gate kept in place under a 2.12 plugin, rejecting every record the new template produced.
#
# So: a repo copy that hashes to one of these lines is an unmodified older release and is
# updated. A copy that hashes to none of them is the repo's and is kept, as before.
#
# Generated from the plugin repo's tags; tools/scripts/shipped-validators-hashes.py appends the
# current tree at each release and a wiring test holds it current. Format: <sha256>  <path>  # <version>
